      "title": "Kemi Badenoch defends selection of man jailed for harassing Jewish MP in council election – UK politics live",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/aug/04/pc-harper-prisoner-early-release-andy-burnham-labour-conservatives-badenoch-latest-news-updates",
      "description": "<p>Conservative leader tells press she stands by decision to select Joshua Bonehill-Paine as a candidate for local election in Somerset</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/aug/03/former-neo-nazi-activist-selected-as-tory-candidate-for-somerset-council-election\">Former neo-Nazi activist selected as Tory candidate for Somerset council election</a></p></li></ul><p>Some 86,495 people were in prison in England and Wales as of 3 August, according to the latest data published by the Ministry of Justice.</p><p>This is 2,026 below the record high of 88,521 reached on 6 September 2024, just before the current early release scheme began.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/aug/04/pc-harper-prisoner-early-release-andy-burnham-labour-conservatives-badenoch-latest-news-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-04T13:19:36"
    },
    {
      "title": "About 1,000 fewer prisoners to get early release as Burnham tightens rules",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/aug/04/fewer-prisoners-early-release-burnham-tightens-rules",
      "description": "<p>Justice secretary says he could not have gone further without causing system to ‘break’ but acknowledges impact on grieving relatives such as those of PC Andrew Harper</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/aug/04/pc-harper-prisoner-early-release-andy-burnham-labour-conservatives-badenoch-latest-news-updates\">UK politics live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>About 1,000 fewer prisoners will be released early after Andy Burnham’s intervention to exclude those convicted of rape, serious child sexual offences and grooming from the scheme.</p><p>The justice secretary, Alex Norris, said 5,000 prisoners would be released over 10 months from October in England and Wales, down from the government’s original plan for 6,000 from September.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/aug/04/fewer-prisoners-early-release-burnham-tightens-rules\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-04T12:18:17"
    },
    {
      "title": "Prisoner early release scheme gives Burnham his first taste of unpopularity",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/aug/04/prisoner-early-release-scheme-burnham-first-taste-unpopularity",
      "description": "<p>After a blitz of small wins, PM is finding that like Keir Starmer there is only so much he can control on the big calls </p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/aug/04/pc-harper-prisoner-early-release-andy-burnham-labour-conservatives-badenoch-latest-news-updates\">UK politics live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>If Andy Burnham wanted to demonstrate he was the anti-Keir Starmer, the first fortnight could not have gone better. Instead of painting a gloomy picture of tough times and an economic black hole that would only improve with sacrifices such as cutting winter fuel allowance, Burnham’s first week was a blitz of small wins including cutting bus fares.</p><p>But the new prime minister can only control so much. And like Starmer, within his first days in office he found himself facing immediate decisions where every call will make you unpopular. And – like Starmer – blaming your predecessor counts for nothing with an angry public.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/aug/04/prisoner-early-release-scheme-burnham-first-taste-unpopularity\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-04T11:23:24"
    }
  ]
